aop: T6040 on 27.2: the firmware's __EDATA region and its ED0p boot argument

The macOS 27.2 AOP firmware also runs initialized data (__EDATA) from
DRAM, which aura (aura-patches/0004) reserves and maps at the IOVA the
firmware uses, inside the external code window that starts at EC0p
(0x10000020000 on the J614s), and takes that IOVA from a new boot
argument, ED0p. iBoot leaves ED0p at 0, as it does EC0p; with 0 the
firmware stalls before it reads its mailbox (the AP's first message
stays unread, nothing comes back) and the start times out (-ETIME).

check_fw_regions() accepted a region only at EC0p or at its physical
address. Accept one region inside the 16 MiB EC0p window too, checked for
its mapping like the others, and pass its IOVA as ED0p. Firmware without
the region (or without ED0p) is unchanged.

